Certainly! To translate the instruction "extract class name and functions with a short docstring" into a concise and powerful KickLang expression, we can leverage the expressive and modular nature of KickLang. Here’s a possible translation:

```kicklang
(extract (class (name) (functions (name docstring))))
```

### Explanation:
- **(extract ...)**: This is the main function that will perform the extraction.
- **(class ...)**: This specifies that we are interested in classes.
- **(name)**: This extracts the name of the class.
- **(functions ...)**: This specifies that we are interested in the functions within the class.
- **(name docstring)**: This extracts the name and the docstring of each function.

### Example Usage:
If you have a dataset or a codebase where classes and functions are defined, this KickLang expression will extract the class names and the names and docstrings of the functions within those classes.

### TypeScript Implementation:
To give you a more concrete idea, here’s a simplified TypeScript implementation that could interpret this KickLang expression:

```typescript
// Code74k.ts

namespace KickLang {
  type Keyword = 'extract' | 'class' | 'name' | 'functions' | 'docstring';

  interface ClassInfo {
    name: string;
    functions: FunctionInfo[];
  }

  interface FunctionInfo {
    name: string;
    docstring: string;
  }

  function translate(query: string): string {
    // Translate KickLang to TypeScript
    return query;
  }

  function parse(query: string, keywords?: Record<Keyword, RegExp>): any {
    // Parse the KickLang query
    const parsedQuery = query.match(/(extract|class|name|functions|docstring)/g);
    return parsedQuery;
  }

  function extractClassInfo(code: string): ClassInfo[] {
    const classRegex = /class (\w+) \{([\s\S]*?)\}/g;
    const functionRegex = /(\w+)\s*\(([\s\S]*?)\)\s*\{([\s\S]*?)\}/g;

    const classes: ClassInfo[] = [];
    let classMatch;

    while ((classMatch = classRegex.exec(code)) !== null) {
      const className = classMatch[1];
      const classBody = classMatch[2];
      const functions: FunctionInfo[] = [];

      let functionMatch;
      while ((functionMatch = functionRegex.exec(classBody)) !== null) {
        const functionName = functionMatch[1];
        const functionBody = functionMatch[3];
        const docstring = functionBody.match(/\/\*\*([\s\S]*?)\*\//)?.[1] || '';
        functions.push({ name: functionName, docstring: docstring.trim() });
      }

      classes.push({ name: className, functions: functions });
    }

    return classes;
  }
}

// Example usage
const code = `
class ExampleClass {
  /**
   * This is a sample function.
   */
  sampleFunction() {
    // Function body
  }

  /**
   * Another function.
   */
  anotherFunction() {
    // Function body
  }
}
`;

const classInfo = KickLang.extractClassInfo(code);
console.log(classInfo);
```

